atlas database-bridge

architecture database-bridge
  canonical_name DatabaseBridge
  family external
  domain Database interoperability
  layer native
  semantic_question Did the selected table rows arrive at the destination with matching values, and what types changed?
  purpose Move table records through DuckDB SQLite, MySQL and PostgreSQL connectors and compare both endpoints after the move; and, for a migration that renames or retypes, map a source schema by cited upstream casting rules and measure a rehearsal against it.
  maturity implemented
  command bonfyre bridge db
  command bonfyre bridge db-verify
  internal_calculus endpoint parsing -> connector attachment -> selected source tables -> optional target copy -> column alignment -> independent row counts and summed field hashes -> comparison receipt
  invariant source attachments are read-only; verification and post-copy readback also attach the destination read-only
  invariant a missing SQLite verification destination is refused without creating a database file
  invariant each column is a separate hash argument after text conversion; SQL NULL remains distinct from a NUL character and field separators cannot merge column boundaries
  invariant existing destination tables are retained unless the caller explicitly supplies --replace
  forbidden_inference matching counts and aggregate hashes -> collision-free equality, a consistent cross-database snapshot, copied constraints or indexes, application compatibility, authorization or a completed migration
  known_gap row hashes are aggregated and are not a cryptographic proof; values compare after text conversion, type changes are reported separately, and the two reads do not share a source/destination transaction
  known_gap DuckDB hash behavior may change between versions; both endpoints are compared using the same installed engine during each invocation
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBridge/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBridge/tests/db_bridge_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreBridge/tests/db_bridge_test.sh verifies SQLite transfer, changed values and missing rows, unchanged files during verification, absent destination refusal, separator and NULL/NUL differences, and optionally real MariaDB/PostgreSQL round trips
  command bonfyre bridge rules
  command bonfyre bridge schema-map
  command bonfyre bridge map-verify
  internal_calculus rules: allowed HTTP 200 ForeignTwin receipt + retained body rehashed to its content_sha256 (or a vendored upstream file, said as such) -> pgloader "Default ... Casting Rules" lines or Frappe self.type_map entries -> rule candidates with exact byte ranges -> sealed rules.json (rules_digest)
  internal_calculus schema-map: SQLite source read-only (pragma table_info, foreign keys, unique indexes, CHECK count, views, triggers) + authored transform plan (bonfyre.bridge.transform-plan.v1: renames, value maps, prefixes, Frappe DocType target, probes) + sealed rules (+ BonfyreFrappeCompiler SchemaIR) -> each column typed by a cited rule or a named exception -> sealed mapping.json (mapping_digest) and optional rehearsal SQL for a throwaway target
  internal_calculus map-verify: sealed mapping + SQLite source + rehearsal target (SQLite, or PostgreSQL read through psql with PGTZ=UTC) -> transforms applied to source values -> canonical text per compare kind -> rows matched by mapped key -> per-column sha256 checksums, row counts, missing/extra/differing keys, declared target types, constraint counts, views/triggers by name, probe queries run in each engine's own dialect -> map-verify receipt with diff_digest; --expect re-checks an earlier receipt and exits 4 on drift
  invariant rules refuses a receipt that is not policy allow with HTTP 200 and a retained body that no longer hashes to the receipt; every rule excerpt is the exact recorded byte range
  invariant a mapping or rules file that no longer matches its own sealed digest is refused by schema-map, map-verify and bonfyre-brief cited
  invariant a column no cited rule covers is carried as text and named unmapped-type; views, triggers and CHECK constraints the rehearsal SQL does not rewrite are named not-carried and check-not-carried
  invariant map-verify never writes either side; an unreachable or unreadable target table reports rows, types and constraints as not matching
  invariant the receipt's display of a PostgreSQL target never carries its password
  forbidden_inference a schema mapping typed by pgloader's documented casting rules -> pgloader having run, or pgloader's using-functions having been applied; the bridge writes its own rehearsal SQL and records the using-function names only
  forbidden_inference a map-verify receipt over the in-repo fixtures -> anything about a customer database; it covers the copy it names and nothing else
  forbidden_inference an Odoo-to-ERPNext Customer rehearsal on SQLite -> ERPNext accepting the records (controllers, naming series, permissions, Link targets and MariaDB strict mode are not exercised)
  known_gap transformation evidence covers SQLite sources only; PostgreSQL is a rehearsal target, MariaDB/MySQL and Oracle/SQL Server are neither sources nor targets of map-verify yet
  known_gap rule sources parsed today: pgloader docs/ref/sqlite.rst (observed) and Frappe mariadb type_map (vendored, not observed); SQLines, ora2pg, OpenUpgrade analysis files and SQLGlot dialect rules are not parsed, and stored procedures, permissions and CDC cutover are not mapped
  known_gap canonical comparison drops trailing zeros and timestamp fraction zeros; values are compared as canonical text, so a precision change that keeps the same canonical text is not seen
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBridge/src/transform.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBridge/tests/transform_evidence_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBridge/tests/fixtures/transform
  witness cmd/BonfyreBridge/tests/transform_evidence_test.sh (make -C cmd/BonfyreBridge test, 2026-10-30) passes 37 checks: 18 pgloader casting rules from the retained ForeignTwin observation open-doc-pgloader-ref-sqlite with exact byte ranges, refused changed body and refused deny receipt, Frappe VARCHAR_LEN resolved to varchar(140); a 4-table SQLite shop mapped 20/20 columns to PostgreSQL and rehearsed on a throwaway PostgreSQL 16 cluster (rows and values match; CHECK, view and trigger named; LIKE 'a%' differs 1;2; vs 1;); a changed value, a deleted row and a retyped column each located and the --expect re-check exits 4; forged mapping refused; password kept out of the receipt; Odoo res_partner mapped onto the compiled ERPNext Customer DocType with Select options and required fields checked, rehearsed and matched on SQLite, and value-map drift located by key
  witness 2026-10-30 live run retained under output/migration-evidence-20261030 (gitignored): rules from receipt open-doc-pgloader-ref-sqlite-20261030T172509Z-e82d3ccd65.json, Frappe rules from integrations/frappe-bench/apps/frappe (8d9f8321), Customer from ~/.bonfyre/frappe-packs/erpnext/schema-ir.json; PostgreSQL 16.15 diff 317326481ca2 and SQLite ERP diff 3202a22e20b5 each re-checked unchanged

interaction database-bridge-evidence-to-cmd-brief
  source database-bridge
  destination cmd-brief
  relation receipt_citation
  preserves sealed mapping_digest, diff_digest, rule excerpts with byte ranges and their ForeignTwin receipt names, per-table row counts and checksums, verdict flags and exceptions
  drops the rehearsal endpoints' authority; the brief cites receipts and never re-runs or upgrades them
  forbidden_inference a brief that cites a rehearsal receipt -> a verified criterion; criteria stay verified false and name the receipt as rehearsal_evidence
  invalidates_on map-verify or schema-map receipt schema, the seal, or the brief's evidence reader changing
  binding cmd/BonfyreBridge/src/transform.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreBrief/src/evidence.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreBrief/tests/cited_brief_test.sh

interaction cli-invokes-database-bridge
  source cmd-c-l-i
  destination database-bridge
  relation native_command_dispatch
  preserves explicit endpoint references, selected tables, move versus verify mode, replacement choice and native exit status
  drops any inference of external account authority from command availability
  forbidden_inference a resolved bridge command -> permission to overwrite the destination or publish a migration claim
  invalidates_on CLI routing, connector behavior or comparison contract changing
  binding cmd/BonfyreCLI/src/main.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreBridge/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreBridge/tests/db_bridge_test.sh
